A region records the weather for 7 consecutive days. Each day's weather is represented by an integer:

1 indicates a sunny day.

0 indicates a rainy day.

The weather report is considered Good if the number of sunny days is strictly greater than the number of rainy days.

Given the weather for all 7 days, determine whether the weather report is Good.

Input Format
A single line containing 7 space-separated integers A1 A2 A3 A4 A5 A6 A7.

Ai = 1 denotes a sunny day

Ai = 0 denotes a rainy day.

Output Format
Print "YES" if the weather report is Good; otherwise print "NO".




#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n=7;
    int a[n];
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        cin>>a[i];
    }
    int s=0;
    int r=0;
   for(int i=0;i<7;i++){
       if(a[i]==1){
           s++;
       }
       if(a[i]==0){
           r++;
       }
   }
   if(s>r){
       cout<<"YES";
   }
   else{
       cout<<"NO";
   }
    return 0;
}
